cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it using the metadata from this file. The associated manuscript is in preparation."
type: software
title: "Phylogeography and cryptic lineages of Cenococcum geophilum in Europe: analysis code"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a study of population structure, cryptic lineages and
  niches of the ectomycorrhizal fungus Cenococcum geophilum across Europe.
  The scripts take whole-genome short reads of several hundred European
  isolates to call variants on a reference built from single-copy
  orthologues, identify/correct clones and describe population structure and
  phylogeny, delimit lineages with several independent lines of evidence,
  and describe diversity, clonality, recombination and the soil and climate
  niches of these lineages.
authors:
  - family-names: Zimmermann
    given-names: Felix
    affiliation: "Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research WSL, Birmensdorf, Switzerland"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0762-2454"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nnamremmizxilef/2026_Cgeophilum_phylogeography"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - Cenococcum geophilum
  - ectomycorrhizal fungi
  - phylogeography
  - cryptic lineages
  - species delimitation
  - population genomics
  - phylogenomics
  - soil niche
